<title>USA: Polaroid sees $25 mln Q4 charge for Sterling.</title>
<headline>Polaroid sees $25 mln Q4 charge for Sterling.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polaroid Corp said on Wednesday it expected to take a $25 million charge in the fourth quarter as part of a sales, marketing and development deal with Sterling Dry Imaging Systems Inc.</p>
<p>The company said it completed previously announced agreements with Sterling, for the sale of some assets and product development cooperation, but it expected to take a charge for severance, inventory, fixed-asset write-offs and other costs.</p>
</text>
